# Organic Driven Development working documents.
#
# `odd/tasks/<feature>.md` is a process artifact: which work unit is in
# flight, what is blocked, what the next session should do. It is written
# and read constantly and it changes on every work unit, so committing it
# puts churn in the diff that says nothing about the product.
#
# The authoritative copy is the Engram observation at
# `odd/<feature>/tasks`, which holds the FULL document, not a summary.
# Engram already outlives a session and a compaction; a file in the working
# tree does not.
#
# The reasoning is not lost. A "why" belongs next to the code it explains,
# where it cannot drift, so it lives in KDoc — see
# `engine/model/.../value/CanonicalNumbers.kt` for the canonical-numerics
# rationale as the worked example. PLAN.md stays committed because it is
# the spec, not the process.
odd/

